4.4. BERT
BERT is the world’s first pre-trained bidirectional and entirely unsupervised language representation approach, having been trained on a massive English Wikipedia corpus [4]. It is an Open-Source Language Representation Model developed by Google AI. Prior to training, BERT can read the texts (or a series of words) in either direction, which is superior to a single-direction technique. BERT surpasses all other word embedding algorithms with fine-tuning, attaining state-of-the-results (SOTA) in multiple NLP applications. BERT

