The sub-sampling layer is another name for the pooling layer. The proposed method employs the 1D max-pooling layer following the 1D convolutional layer and batch normalization layer, which performs a downsampling operation on the features to reduce their size [48]. It collects small rectangular data chunks and produces a distinct output for each piece. This can be performed in a variety of different methods. In this study, the Maxpooling approach is used to find the largest value in a set of neighboring inputs. The pooling of a feature map inside a layer is defined by (12) [49]:

